;; a program under the naming law through the bridge (LANGUAGE.md §8.6 slice 4.4 landing 1): its
;; World, its extern over ByteArray, its string literal over Init's List. The chain's string is
;; its reader's Cons and Nil, and Init's List is identified with the chain's prelude by the
;; emitter, so the literal needs no rewrite. A naming-law case lives at the root (no kernel/
;; directory) and its reference under the tie is the V3 driver's --run, never the bootstrap's
;; flat read, which reads an unknown head as an effect and `-` at Nat as the integer's
(import Init String.toByteArray)
(type World (World Nat))
(extern write_line ((bytes ByteArray) (w World)) World)
(fn main ((w World)) World (write_line (String.toByteArray "hello") w))
